WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:03.950
The two models persisted for at least 50 years,

00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:08.850
in part because it was really hard to test which of the two models was correct.

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:15.370
So when you think about it,

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:20.100
what you're trying to ask is what caused a new trait to appear?

00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:24.110
Did the environment cause the trait to appear?

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:28.450
Or did the trait appear first and the environment simply selected upon the trait?

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:30.490
So you can think in your lifetime,

00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:30.780
you know,

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:34.950
most of the traits we see out there are preexisting,

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:40.140
and so you needed a situation where you had a population of 

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:43.220
individuals where the trait didn't exist.

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:44.530
So that was the number one challenge.

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:45.160
For example,

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:50.150
let's say we're looking for a trait for humans to have purple hair, and 

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:51.500
nobody has purple hair.

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:51.780
So,

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:53.010
that's what you start with.

00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:53.620
And then you can say,

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:53.960
okay,

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:56.920
now I'm going to see, when did the purple hair appear?

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.550
I'm going to actually visualize the appearance of the purple hair.

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:00.360
And then,

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:01.190
if I visualize it,

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:05.570
I can ask well did it happen before or after something that would make purple hair be 

00:01:05.650 --> 00:01:06.450
advantageous.

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:09.410
So in that model we have three components.

00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:14.310
We first have to have a population which didn't have purple hair to start with, the appearance of purple hair has to be 

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:18.520
frequent enough that it happens in our lifetime, so we have to be able to observe it 

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:19.460
experimentally,

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:20.600
and third,

00:01:20.610 --> 00:01:25.180
we have to be able to show whether that trait happened before or after the 

00:01:25.370 --> 00:01:26.950
environmental change happened.

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:29.050
So did it happen in the absence of any environmental change?

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:31.600
Or did it happen as a response to environmental change?

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:35.450
So we're stuck with this conundrum of 

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:39.320
first observing something new that nobody's ever seen before,

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:42.770
having it happen in a timely fashion that we can observe it happen, and third,

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:48.050
being able to determine when it happened relative to any potential environmental change.

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:53.500
So those were the conundrums, the problem that faced them, and there were a lot of crazy 

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:54.280
experiments done.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:56.200
Lamarckians did things like,

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:56.410
you know,

00:01:56.750 --> 00:02:01.183
chopping off the tails of mice and then seeing if the baby mice had shorter tails 

00:02:01.703 --> 00:02:04.143
and, you know, the answer was they didn't.

00:02:04.633 --> 00:02:06.323
But then you could argue, well,

00:02:06.653 --> 00:02:11.383
they really just didn't do enough mice to be able to see the rare mice that could've responded to the environmental 

00:02:11.383 --> 00:02:11.843
change.

00:02:12.983 --> 00:02:16.593
And so they-- and it wasn't really an appearance of a new trait.

00:02:16.733 --> 00:02:19.883
Then there are other examples of where a new trait appears,

00:02:21.163 --> 00:02:25.143
like a human breaks its arm,

00:02:25.903 --> 00:02:27.863
but that's not really a heritable trait,

00:02:27.863 --> 00:02:31.633
it's just something that caused damage to the organism.

00:02:31.713 --> 00:02:32.473
It's new,

00:02:32.753 --> 00:02:37.343
but it's not really something that changes its genetic material in response to some, you know.

00:02:38.233 --> 00:02:42.993
So, those were the problems that faced and 

00:02:42.993 --> 00:02:46.743
nobody could really find a system that could bring all those characteristics together.

